What is Java:
// Java — platform-independent, object-oriented
public class HelloWorld {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Hello, Java!");
    }
}

// Compile: javac HelloWorld.java  → produces HelloWorld.class bytecode
// Run:     java HelloWorld         → JVM interprets bytecode

// Key characteristics:
// - Statically typed: all variables have a declared type
// - Garbage collected: memory managed automatically
// - JVM-based: bytecode runs anywhere a JVM exists

JDK vs JRE vs JVM:
// Check installed versions from terminal:
// java -version       → shows JRE/JVM version
// javac -version      → shows JDK compiler version
// javac HelloWorld.java  → JDK compiles source → .class bytecode
// java HelloWorld         → JRE executes bytecode

// JDK = JRE + dev tools (compiler, debugger, profiler)
// JRE = JVM + core libraries
// JVM = bytecode interpreter + JIT compiler

